CAT = "s65Advisers"; SEG = "ADV"
Q = [
("Under the SEC's three-part test, a person is an investment adviser if she gives advice about securities, is in the business of doing so, and:", 'Receives compensation', ['Holds client funds', 'Has discretion', 'Manages over 25 accounts'], 'The test asks whether the person advises on securities, is in the business of advising, and is paid for it in any form. Custody and discretion are not part of the definition.'),
('A CPA prepares tax returns and also charges clients a separate fee for advice on which mutual funds to buy. The CPA:', 'Is an investment adviser', ['Is excluded as an accountant', 'Is an agent of the funds', 'Needs no state filing at all'], 'The professional exclusion covers only advice that is solely incidental to the practice. Charging a separate fee for securities advice makes the CPA an investment adviser.'),
('Under the Uniform Securities Act, which of these is an investment adviser?', 'A pension consultant paid for fund advice', ["A bank's trust department", 'A teacher in a college finance class', "A newspaper's personal finance columnist"], 'Consultants paid to advise pension plans on securities choices are advisers. Banks, teachers whose advice is incidental, and publishers of general-circulation papers are excluded.'),
('A broker-dealer agent recommends stocks to customers and is paid only commissions on the trades. The agent:', 'Is not an adviser', ['Must register as an IAR', 'Must register as an adviser', 'Must charge an advisory fee'], "A broker-dealer's advice that is incidental to its brokerage business, with no special compensation, is excluded. A separate advisory fee would change that."),
('A publisher sells a newsletter of general circulation with stock picks, plus a phone line giving personal advice for an extra fee. The phone service:', 'Makes the publisher an adviser', ['Is covered by the press exclusion', 'Is exempt as a publication', 'Needs only an SEC filing'], "The publisher exclusion covers impersonal, regularly published content of general circulation. Advice tailored to each caller's situation is investment advice."),
('An adviser manages a registered mutual fund with modest assets. It must register:', 'With the SEC', ['With each state where it does business', 'With FINRA', 'Nowhere, as it is exempt'], 'Any adviser to a registered investment company is a federal covered adviser and registers with the SEC regardless of its assets under management.'),
('An SEC-registered adviser has a place of business in a state. Under NSMIA, the state may require the firm itself to:', 'Notice file and pay a fee', ['Register with the state', 'Keep extra books and records', 'Meet a state net worth test'], "NSMIA bars states from registering federal covered advisers or adding books, records, net capital or bonding rules, but a state may require a notice filing (copies of Form ADV), a fee and consent to service of process."),
('A state-registered adviser has no office in another state, and its only clients there are two insurance companies. In that state it:', 'Need not register', ['Must register now', 'Must notice file', 'Must register its IARs'], "An adviser with no place of business in a state whose only clients there are institutions, such as insurers and banks, falls outside the state's registration requirement."),
('An adviser opens a branch office in a state but has only one client there so far. It:', 'Must register in that state', ['Is exempt as de minimis', 'Need only notify the SEC', 'May wait for a sixth client'], 'The de minimis exemption requires having no place of business in the state. Once the adviser has an office there, it must register whatever its client count.'),
("An adviser's employee writes the research that tells IARs which securities to recommend, but never speaks with clients. She is:", 'An IAR', ['Excluded as back-office staff', 'An agent', 'An investment adviser'], 'The IAR definition covers anyone who determines which recommendation or advice should be given, not only those who meet clients.'),
('An adviser has $40 million of assets under management and its only office in one state. It generally registers with:', 'Its home state', ['The SEC', 'FINRA', 'Every state with clients'], 'Under the Investment Advisers Act, advisers below the $100 million mid-sized threshold generally register with their home state, not the SEC, unless an exception applies.'),
('An adviser registered with the SEC makes a notice filing in a state. Which person working there may the state require to register?', 'An IAR with an office there', ["The firm's outside auditor", 'Its chief financial officer', 'A clerk who mails statements'], 'States may register the IARs of federal covered advisers who have a place of business in the state. Clerical staff and those who give no advice are not IARs.'),
("A client must be given the education, business background and disciplinary history of the IAR who advises her. This is in:", 'Form ADV Part 2B', ['Form ADV Part 1A', 'Form U5', 'Form BD'], "Part 2B, the brochure supplement, describes the individuals who give advice. Part 2A is the firm's brochure, Part 1 goes to regulators, and Form U5 records an individual's termination."),
('A state-registered adviser moves its main office to a new address. It must:', 'Promptly amend Form ADV', ['Wait for its annual update', 'Notify clients only', 'File a new registration'], "Material changes, including the firm's address, require a prompt Form ADV amendment. Other changes can wait for the annual updating amendment."),
("A state-registered adviser's annual updating amendment to Form ADV is due within how long after its fiscal year end?", '90 days', ['30 days', '120 days', '60 days'], 'Advisers file an annual updating amendment within 90 days after the end of their fiscal year, in addition to any prompt amendments during the year.'),
('Which of these is among the books and records a state-registered adviser must keep?', 'A memo of each order placed', ["Clients' personal tax returns", 'Recordings of every phone call', "Employees' credit reports"], "NASAA's recordkeeping rule requires a memorandum of each order given by the adviser for a client, along with journals, ledgers, client contracts and written communications about advice."),
("An IAR at a state-registered firm executes trades contrary to the firm's procedures. Under state rules, the adviser:", 'Must supervise her', ['Has no duty for her acts', 'Must report only to FINRA', 'Is liable only if it profited'], 'An adviser must reasonably supervise its IARs and enforce written procedures. Failure to supervise is grounds for action against the firm itself.'),
('A firm advises only venture capital funds and is not registered with the SEC, but files reports with it. It is:', 'An exempt reporting adviser', ['A federal covered adviser', 'A registered broker-dealer', 'An issuer of securities'], 'Advisers to only venture capital funds, and small private fund advisers, are exempt from SEC registration but file parts of Form ADV as exempt reporting advisers.'),
('A sports agent charges a pro athlete a fee to recommend which stocks and bonds to buy. The agent is:', 'An investment adviser', ['Excluded as an agent', 'An issuer agent', 'Exempt as a professional'], 'Anyone in the business of giving securities advice for compensation is an adviser. Sports and entertainment agents are not on the list of excluded professionals.'),
('A sole proprietor adviser incorporates and carries on the same advisory business. To avoid a gap, the new corporation may:', 'File as a successor', ['Use the old registration', 'Stop advising for a year', 'Notify only its clients'], "A successor that takes over a registered adviser's business may file for registration as a successor, so the business continues without a lapse."),
]
